['weekly_sales', 'shopping_cart_users', 'bitcoin_members', 'interest_metrics', 'customer_regions', 'customer_transactions', 'bitcoin_transactions', 'customer_nodes', 'cleaned_weekly_sales', 'veg_txn_df', 'shopping_cart_events', 'shopping_cart_page_hierarchy', 'bitcoin_prices', 'interest_map', 'veg_loss_rate_df', 'shopping_cart_campaign_identifier', 'veg_cat', 'veg_whsle_df', 'shopping_cart_event_identifier']
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant tables, columns and how they will be used  

• shopping_cart_events."page_id": link every recorded event to a page ( = a SKU page when the row exists in shopping_cart_page_hierarchy).  
• shopping_cart_events."event_type": numeric flag that tells us whether the row is a 1‑Page View, 2‑Add to Cart or 3‑Purchase.  
• shopping_cart_page_hierarchy."page_id": joins to shopping_cart_events to look‑up the product behind the page.  
• shopping_cart_page_hierarchy."product_id": the real “product” key we ultimately want to report on.  
• shopping_cart_page_hierarchy."page_name": handy label for the product (optional in the output).  
• shopping_cart_event_identifier."event_type": joins to shopping_cart_events so we can decode the numbers.  
• shopping_cart_event_identifier."event_name": the human readable event (“Page View”, “Add to Cart”, “Purchase”).  

Primary filter that will be applied everywhere  
shopping_cart_events."page_id" NOT IN (1,2,12,13)    -- remove the Home page, All‑Products page, and any other specified pages.  

Below are ten exploratory → progressively‑complex SQLite queries (each capped with LIMIT 20) to understand the data and to build up to the final answer.  

```sql
-- 1️⃣ Description: Show the event‑type reference table to understand the numeric codes
SELECT *
FROM "shopping_cart_event_identifier"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2️⃣ Description: List all product pages (excluding the filtered page_ids) and their product_ids
SELECT DISTINCT "page_id",
       "page_name",
       "product_id"
FROM "shopping_cart_page_hierarchy"
WHERE "page_id" NOT IN (1,2,12,13)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3️⃣ Description: Peek at raw events for one product page (e.g., first non‑filtered page_id)  
SELECT *
FROM "shopping_cart_events"
WHERE "page_id" NOT IN (1,2,12,13)
  AND "page_id" = (SELECT MIN("page_id")
                   FROM "shopping_cart_page_hierarchy"
                   WHERE "page_id" NOT IN (1,2,12,13))
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4️⃣ Description: Count page‑views (event_type = 1) for every product_id
SELECT h."product_id",
       COUNT(*) AS "views"
FROM   "shopping_cart_events"  AS e
JOIN   "shopping_cart_page_hierarchy" AS h
       ON e."page_id" = h."page_id"
WHERE  e."event_type" = 1
  AND  e."page_id" NOT IN (1,2,12,13)
GROUP  BY h."product_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5️⃣ Description: Count add‑to‑cart events (event_type = 2) for every product_id
SELECT h."product_id",
       COUNT(*) AS "adds_to_cart"
FROM   "shopping_cart_events"  AS e
JOIN   "shopping_cart_page_hierarchy" AS h
       ON e."page_id" = h."page_id"
WHERE  e."event_type" = 2
  AND  e."page_id" NOT IN (1,2,12,13)
GROUP  BY h."product_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6️⃣ Description: Count completed purchases (event_type = 3) for every product_id
SELECT h."product_id",
       COUNT(*) AS "purchases"
FROM   "shopping_cart_events"  AS e
JOIN   "shopping_cart_page_hierarchy" AS h
       ON e."page_id" = h."page_id"
WHERE  e."event_type" = 3
  AND  e."page_id" NOT IN (1,2,12,13)
GROUP  BY h."product_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7️⃣ Description: One table with all three event counts using conditional aggregation
SELECT h."product_id",
       SUM(CASE WHEN e."event_type" = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "views",
       SUM(CASE WHEN e."event_type" = 2 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "adds_to_cart",
       SUM(CASE WHEN e."event_type" = 3 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "purchases"
FROM   "shopping_cart_events"  AS e
JOIN   "shopping_cart_page_hierarchy" AS h
       ON e."page_id" = h."page_id"
WHERE  e."page_id" NOT IN (1,2,12,13)
GROUP  BY h."product_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8️⃣ Description: Extend previous query to calculate “left in cart” (adds – purchases)
SELECT h."product_id",
       SUM(CASE WHEN e."event_type" = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "views",
       SUM(CASE WHEN e."event_type" = 2 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "adds_to_cart",
       SUM(CASE WHEN e."event_type" = 3 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "purchases",
       SUM(CASE WHEN e."event_type" = 2 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)
       - SUM(CASE WHEN e."event_type" = 3 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "left_in_cart"
FROM   "shopping_cart_events"  AS e
JOIN   "shopping_cart_page_hierarchy" AS h
       ON e."page_id" = h."page_id"
WHERE  e."page_id" NOT IN (1,2,12,13)
GROUP  BY h."product_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9️⃣ Description: Same as #8 but also show the readable page_name for context
SELECT h."product_id",
       h."page_name",
       SUM(CASE WHEN e."event_type" = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "views",
       SUM(CASE WHEN e."event_type" = 2 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "adds_to_cart",
       SUM(CASE WHEN e."event_type" = 3 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "purchases",
       SUM(CASE WHEN e."event_type" = 2 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)
       - SUM(CASE WHEN e."event_type" = 3 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "left_in_cart"
FROM   "shopping_cart_events"  AS e
JOIN   "shopping_cart_page_hierarchy" AS h
       ON e."page_id" = h."page_id"
WHERE  e."page_id" NOT IN (1,2,12,13)
GROUP  BY h."product_id", h."page_name"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 🔟 Description: Final full breakdown ordered by highest page views
SELECT h."product_id",
       h."page_name",
       COUNT(CASE WHEN e."event_type" = 1 THEN 1 END) AS "views",
       COUNT(CASE WHEN e."event_type" = 2 THEN 1 END) AS "adds_to_cart",
       COUNT(CASE WHEN e."event_type" = 3 THEN 1 END) AS "purchases",
       COUNT(CASE WHEN e."event_type" = 2 THEN 1 END)
       - COUNT(CASE WHEN e."event_type" = 3 THEN 1 END) AS "left_in_cart"
FROM   "shopping_cart_events"  AS e
JOIN   "shopping_cart_page_hierarchy" AS h
       ON e."page_id" = h."page_id"
WHERE  e."page_id" NOT IN (1,2,12,13)
GROUP  BY h."product_id", h."page_name"
ORDER  BY "views" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```
